IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pea-types`

-- Protection from Eviction Act 1977 (UK) — GOAL 1: EVICTION ONLY BY COURT
-- PROCEEDINGS (ss 2, 3, 3A, 8).
--
--   "Must the owner go to court to recover possession from this occupier?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-1977-43.txt — ss 2, 3, 3A, 8.

§ `Goal 1 — eviction only by court proceedings`

-- s 3A(2)-(8): the exclusions. (8) applies to a licence only.
@ref s 3A(2)-(8)
GIVEN o IS AN `Occupancy`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the facts make it excluded under s 3A` o IF
        x's `shares with a resident landlord`
    OR  x's `shares with a resident member of the landlord's family, landlord in the same building`
    OR  x's `granted as a temporary expedient to a trespasser`
    OR  x's `for a holiday only`
    OR  x's `granted otherwise than for money or money's worth`
    OR  x's `asylum support accommodation`
    OR  x's `an immigration-barred residential tenancy agreement`
    OR  (x's `a hostel licence from a listed body` AND isLicence)
    WHERE
        x MEANS o's `exclusions`
        isLicence MEANS
            CONSIDER o's `kind`
            WHEN `a licence` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 3(2C) "References in the preceding provisions of this section ... to an
-- excluded tenancy do not apply to— (a) a tenancy entered into before the
-- date on which the Housing Act 1988 came into force, or (b) a tenancy
-- entered into on or after that date but pursuant to a contract made before
-- that date". The saving is for tenancies; an excluded licence is excluded
-- whenever granted.
@ref ss 3(2C), 3A, 8(4)
@export Whether a tenancy or licence is excluded under s 3A of the Protection from Eviction Act 1977 (UK), for ss 3 and 5: it shares accommodation with a resident landlord or (in the same non-purpose-built building) a resident member of the landlord's family, was granted to a trespasser as a temporary expedient, is for a holiday only or not for money, is asylum support or immigration-barred accommodation, or is a hostel licence from a listed body; a tenancy entered into before the Housing Act 1988 (or under an earlier contract) is never excluded. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN o IS AN `Occupancy`  @desc The kind of occupancy, when it was entered into, and the facts behind each exclusion
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is excluded` o IF
        `the facts make it excluded under s 3A` o
    AND NOT savedTenancy
    WHERE
        savedTenancy MEANS
            CONSIDER o's `kind`
            WHEN `a licence` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE o's `entered into before the Housing Act 1988`

-- s 2 "Where any premises are let as a dwelling on a lease which is subject
-- to a right of re-entry or forfeiture it shall not be lawful to enforce that
-- right otherwise than by proceedings in the court while any person is
-- lawfully residing in the premises or part of them."
@ref s 2
GIVEN o IS AN `Occupancy`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 2 requires proceedings to forfeit` o IF
        o's `let or occupied as a dwelling`
    AND isLease
    AND o's `a lease with a right of re-entry or forfeiture`
    AND o's `someone lawfully residing`
    WHERE
        -- Only a lease can carry a right of forfeiture (added after the
        -- independent pass, remark 8).
        isLease MEANS
            CONSIDER o's `kind`
            WHEN `a tenancy` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 3(1) "Where any premises have been let as a dwelling under a tenancy
-- which is neither a statutorily protected tenancy nor an excluded tenancy
-- and— (a) the tenancy ... has come to an end, but (b) the occupier continues
-- to reside in the premises or part of them, it shall not be lawful for the
-- owner to enforce against the occupier, otherwise than by proceedings in the
-- court, his right to recover possession". (2B): the same for premises
-- occupied as a dwelling under a licence other than an excluded licence.
-- s 8(2): exclusive possession under employment is a tenancy for Part I.
@ref s 3(1), (2B), s 8(1)-(2)
GIVEN o IS AN `Occupancy`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3 requires proceedings to recover possession` o IF
        o's `let or occupied as a dwelling`
    AND NOT (o's `statutorily protected`)
    AND NOT (`is excluded` o)
    AND o's `has come to an end`
    AND o's `occupier continues to reside`

@ref ss 2, 3
@export Whether the Protection from Eviction Act 1977 (UK) makes it unlawful for the owner to recover possession (or forfeit) otherwise than by proceedings in the court: s 2 (a dwelling lease with a right of re-entry or forfeiture while anyone lawfully resides there) or s 3 (a tenancy or licence of a dwelling, neither statutorily protected nor excluded, that has ended while the occupier still resides there). FALSE means this Act does not require it; a statutorily protected tenancy is protected by its own Act. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN o IS AN `Occupancy`  @desc The letting, whether it is protected or excluded, whether it has ended and the occupier still resides, and any right of forfeiture
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `court proceedings are required to recover possession from` o IF
        `s 2 requires proceedings to forfeit` o
    OR  `s 3 requires proceedings to recover possession` o
